Hi,
I=E2=80=99m seeing a reproducible kernel WARNING with the rtw88 driver on a=
n
RTL8822BE card. The Wi-Fi card worked normally before a suspend/resume
cycle. Since then, the warning appears during connection attempts, and the
AP never answers authentication frames, so Wi-Fi association fails.
Bluetooth on the same combo card keeps working.

System
Laptop: HP 250 G4 Notebook PC
Wi-Fi: Realtek RTL8822BE 802.11ac [10ec:b822] (Subsystem: Hewlett-Packard),
device 0000:0d:00.0
Bound driver per sysfs: rtw_8822be. Loaded modules: rtw88_8822be,
rtw88_8822b, rtw88_pci, rtw88_core
Bluetooth: same combo card, working (btusb, btrtl, btintel/btbcm/btmtk
loaded for other devices; the RTL Bluetooth function is operational)
Firmware: version 27.2.0, H2C version 13
Kernels tested: 6.14.0-37-generic (Ubuntu 24.04 base, Linux Mint) and
7.0.0-38-generic. The warning appears on both, at different line numbers
(see below).
NetworkManager uses the wpa_supplicant backend.

History
Wi-Fi worked normally after initial setup and was used for regular
connections.
After a suspend/resume cycle, the interface stopped connecting. Scanning
still lists networks, but association fails.
Since then, the failure has persisted across reboots, kernel switches (6.14
and 7.0), and module reloads.

Symptoms
The interface is detected, and scanning works; networks are listed with
full signal.
Connection attempts fail. NetworkManager reports =E2=80=9CWi-Fi network cou=
ld not
be found=E2=80=9D (reason: ssid-not-found).
Affected networks include a 2.4 GHz AP on channel 8 and a 5 GHz AP on
channel 128 (DFS). The regulatory domain is set to UA (DFS-ETSI).
A phone connects to the same access points without issues.
Kernel log on 6.14.0-37-generic during a connection attempt:

WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 3439 at drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/phy.c:2120
rtw_get_tx_power_params+0x579/0x1260 [rtw88_core]
RIP: 0010:rtw_get_tx_power_params+0x579/0x1260 [rtw88_core]
Call Trace:
  rtw_phy_get_tx_power_index+0x4e/0xf0 [rtw88_core]
  rtw_phy_set_tx_power_level+0xe4/0x1f0 [rtw88_core]
  rtw_set_channel+0xbc/0x140 [rtw88_core]
  rtw_ops_config+0x8b/0xe0 [rtw88_core]
wlan0: authenticate with f4:1e:57:e6:a0:77 (local address=3Dd8:12:65:96:44:=
71)
wlan0: send auth to f4:1e:57:e6:a0:77 (try 1/3)
wlan0: send auth to f4:1e:57:e6:a0:77 (try 2/3)
wlan0: send auth to f4:1e:57:e6:a0:77 (try 3/3)
wlan0: authentication with f4:1e:57:e6:a0:77 timed out

The same warning appeared earlier on 7.0.0-38-generic, at phy.c:2213 in
rtw_get_tx_power_params, from the rtw_set_channel path.
The warning fires during connection attempts. In the logs I have, every
attempt that reached rtw_set_channel produced it, and the authentication
frames then went unanswered.

Steps taken
Set the regulatory domain with iw reg set UA. No change.
Tried several access points on different channels, including 2.4 GHz
channel 8 and 5 GHz channel 128. Same result.
Set rtw88_pci disable_aspm=3Dy and rtw88_core disable_lps_deep=3Dy via modp=
robe
options. No change.
Reloaded the rtw88 modules without a reboot. No change.
Switched NetworkManager=E2=80=99s Wi-Fi backend to wpa_supplicant (iwd.serv=
ice was
masked on this system). No change in association behavior.

Questions
Is this a known issue? If so, is there a fix or a debug patch?
Is there a known interaction between suspend/resume and rtw88 channel/TX
power setup on RTL8822BE that could explain why Bluetooth still works while
Wi-Fi association fails?
I can test patches and provide more logs. I can supply the full dmesg, iw
dev, iw list, and lspci -vv -s 0d:00.0.

The full dmesg output is attached as a plain text file.

Thanks,
Dmytro

